---
import Site from '../layouts/Site.astro'

const lastUpdated = 'June 2026'
---

<Site
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How SEQ Campers collects, uses, and protects your personal information when you visit our website, submit quote requests, or make a payment."
>
  <div class="page-header page-header-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>SEQ Campers Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;">
      <div class="rich-text">

        <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
        <p>
          SEQ Campers (we, us, or our) is committed to protecting your privacy and ensuring you have a positive
          experience on our website. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and otherwise
          process your personal information when you visit our website, submit quote requests, subscribe to our
          newsletter, or make deposits and payments.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3>2.1 Information You Provide Directly</h3>
        <p>We collect information you voluntarily provide through our website, including:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact Form Data:</strong> When you submit a quote request or inquiry form, we collect your
            name, email address, phone number, postcode, and details about your camper interests or inquiry.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Newsletter Subscription:</strong> When you subscribe to our newsletter or marketing emails,
            we collect your email address and any other information you provide.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Payment Information:</strong> When you make a deposit or payment:
            <ul>
              <li>
                <em>For online deposits via Stripe:</em> We collect billing name, address, and transaction
                details. Your card information (credit/debit card numbers, expiry dates, CVC codes) is processed
                securely by Stripe, our certified payment processor. We do not store, process, or have access to
                your full card details.
              </li>
              <li>
                <em>For direct bank transfers:</em> We collect transaction confirmation details and bank account
                information you provide to us. This information is used only to reconcile payments and
                communicate with you.
              </li>
            </ul>
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Communications:</strong> If you contact us directly via email or other communication
            channels, we collect the information you include in your message.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2.2 Information Collected Automatically</h3>
        <p>When you visit our website, we may automatically collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Browser and device information (browser type, operating system, device type)</li>
          <li>IP address and general location information</li>
          <li>Usage data (pages visited, time spent, links clicked)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. How We Use Your Information</h2>
        <p>We use the information we collect for the following purposes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>To respond to your inquiry or quote request</li>
          <li>To process and confirm deposits and payments</li>
          <li>To send payment confirmations and invoices</li>
          <li>To send you marketing communications and newsletters (with your consent)</li>
          <li>To improve our website and services</li>
          <li>To prevent fraud and unauthorized transactions (for online payments)</li>
          <li>To comply with legal and tax obligations</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Sharing of Information</h2>
        <p>
          We do not sell, rent, or lease your personal information to third parties. However, we may share your
          information in the following circumstances:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            With Stripe (for online deposits only) to process secure payments and prevent fraud. Stripe is
            PCI-DSS Level 1 compliant. See Stripe's Privacy Policy at
            <a href="https://stripe.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">https://stripe.com/privacy</a>
          </li>
          <li>
            With other service providers who assist us (e.g., email service providers, website hosts) under
            confidentiality agreements
          </li>
          <li>When required by law or legal process</li>
          <li>To protect our rights, privacy, safety, or property</li>
          <li>In connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets (we will notify you of such change)</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Data Security</h2>
        <p>
          We implement reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to protect your personal
          information from unauthorized access, alteration, disclosure, and destruction.
        </p>
        <p>
          For online deposits via Stripe, we use industry-standard encryption (SSL/TLS) and partner with Stripe,
          a Payment Card Industry (PCI) Data Security Standard Level 1 compliant service provider. We never
          store your full credit card details on our systems. For direct bank transfer payments, we protect
          banking information through secure communication channels and restricted access to payment records.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Data Retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain your personal information for as long as necessary to fulfill the purposes outlined in this
          Privacy Policy, unless a longer retention period is required by law. For quote requests, we typically
          retain information for 12 months. For payment records, invoices, and transaction details (whether via
          Stripe or direct transfer), we retain information for 7 years to comply with Australian tax law and
          accounting standards. Newsletter subscribers can have their information retained until they unsubscribe.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Your Rights</h2>
        <p>Under Australian Privacy Law, you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Access the personal information we hold about you</li>
          <li>Request correction of inaccurate information</li>
          <li>Opt-out of marketing communications at any time</li>
          <li>Request deletion of your information (subject to legal obligations)</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, please contact us using the details provided in Section 9. For
          payment-related data held by Stripe, please contact Stripe directly at
          <a href="mailto:privacy@stripe.com">privacy@stripe.com</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Marketing Communications</h2>
        <p>
          If you subscribe to our newsletter or marketing emails, we will use your email address to send you
          updates, promotions, and information about our products and services.
        </p>
        <p>You can unsubscribe from marketing communications at any time by:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Clicking the Unsubscribe link in any email we send you</li>
          <li>Contacting us directly at the email address or phone number below</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>9. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, wish to access or correct your information, or want
          to exercise your privacy rights, please contact us:
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>SEQ Campers</strong><br />
          Email: <a href="mailto:admin@seqcampers.com.au">admin@seqcampers.com.au</a><br />
          Phone: <a href="tel:0753707933">07 5370 7933</a><br />
          Address: 3B/6 Bonanza Court, Marcoola QLD 4564
        </p>

        <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices, technology,
          legal requirements, or other factors. We will notify you of any material changes by posting the
          updated Privacy Policy on our website and updating the Last Updated date.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Compliance</h2>
        <p>
          This Privacy Policy is designed to comply with the Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy
          Principles (APPs), as well as other applicable privacy and data protection laws.
        </p>

        <p style="margin-top:32px; color:var(--muted); font-size:0.88rem;">
          &copy; 2026 SEQ Campers. All rights reserved.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Site>
